;;; The alive-∅ record site at PHASE 1 — a state the engine called a model and
;;; its own rules refute. **Fixed** at M1e S1e.3.1 (`CO-M1`); this is the
;;; regression. Found and banked 2026-08-28 as M1e D1.
;;
;; `phase1` checked `has_contradiction(root)` at solve.rs:1091, then called
;; `compute_alive` — which writes the lookahead kill cache INTO ROOT
;; (hypgen.rs `write_negated`) — and then recorded root under the comment
;; "Empty alive and no contradiction ⇒ root is itself a complete, consistent
;; model". **The check ran before the write.**
;;
;; Zero enterings, zero layers, one saturation, and the state it recorded as
;; the model was one in which `totality` matched and had not fired: feed that
;; model back in as a program and this engine answers `Contradiction`.
;;
;; `record_node` now re-saturates a KB written since its last saturation and
;; declines to record one its own rules refute, so this file answers
;; `Contradiction` — which is also what `-L` said all along, and what a hand
;; derivation says.
;;
;; `-K` is the discriminator on the **old** behaviour and is kept because it
;; still shows the mechanism: with the kill cache off, root keeps no negatives,
;; `totality` has nothing to read, and the state is a genuine solution. So the
;; two configurations answer differently, and that is a fact about the program
;; rather than about the read-out.
;;
;; ── The `:expect`, and Q-M1e.13 ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;
;; The banked claim was `(model (is-a A T) (is-a B T))` with the goal moved off
;; `p`, because an expectation must name the goal's relations and the recorded
;; model contained no `p` fact at all — Q-M1e.13. `(false)` names nothing, so
;; the fix removes the need for the workaround and the goal goes back to the
;; question the file is about. Q-M1e.13 itself is still open.

(relation is-a T T)
(relation p T)

(is-a A T) (is-a B T)

;; One candidate per object — reads only `is-a`, so the kill cache it triggers
;; is not a fact this generator conditions on.
(hrule guess () :match (is-a ?x T) :assert (p ?x))

;; One step from any (p ?x), so the pre-branch lookahead kills every candidate
;; and the cache writes (not (p A)) / (not (p B)) into root.
(rule no-p () :match (p ?x) :assert (false) :priority 300)

;; Totality, on stored negatives alone — no `absent`, so no NAF boundary is in
;; the argument. Dormant while root is saturated; refuting once the cache has
;; written. Root is not re-saturated, so it never fires.
(rule totality ()
  :match  (and (not (p A)) (not (p B)))
  :assert (false)
  :priority 400)

(query
  :goal   (p ?x)
  :expect (false))
